---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import EmailSignup from "../components/EmailSignup.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="Who Pearl Davis is and what JustPearlyThings and The Audacity Network are about.">
  <span class="pill">The official page</span>
  <h1>Pearl Davis</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Host of JustPearlyThings. Founder of The Audacity Network. Pearl reports on
    dating, family, and the family-court system on YouTube, podcasts, and in
    documentary work — focused on what men, fathers, and families actually
    experience inside those institutions. This site is her official home on the web.
  </p>

  <div class="grid cols-2">
    <div class="card center">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">2M+</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        YouTube subscribers on
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@JustPearlyThings" rel="noopener">@JustPearlyThings</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card center">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Since 2020</h3>
      <p class="muted">Producing independently across social, podcast, and long-form.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>One person, several properties</h2>
  <p>
    Everything official routes through here. <strong>JustPearlyThings</strong> is the
    show — free episodes and clips on
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@JustPearlyThings" rel="noopener">YouTube</a> and
    Rumble, plus the Pearl Daily podcast.
    <a href="https://theaudacitynetwork.com" rel="noopener">The Audacity Network</a> is
    the paid product — every episode, live streams, exclusive documentaries, and the
    members' community. <a href="https://justpearlymerch.com" rel="noopener">Justpearlymerch</a>
    is the store. If a page or account isn't linked from this site, it isn't official.
  </p>

  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>
    A creator whose distribution belongs to someone else can be silenced by a policy
    change. That has happened to this channel repeatedly across TikTok, Instagram, and
    YouTube. This site is the version of the operation that isn't hosted on anyone else's
    platform — an address that can't be reassigned, a mailing list that can't be
    throttled, and a durable record of the reporting even when the underlying videos are
    removed elsewhere. It is also the public layer around the paid product: what the
    network covers, why, where the money goes, and where every claim gets its citation.
  </p>

  <h2>The mission</h2>
  <p>
    Cover what happens to men and families inside modern dating, marriage, and the
    family-court system — a beat mainstream outlets have underweighted for a generation.
    Publish sources next to claims. Keep the record durable even when the algorithm
    decides otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>Press, booking &amp; contact</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      For interview requests, debate invitations, event booking, press, and business
      inquiries, email
      <a href="mailto:production@theaudacitynetwork.com">production@theaudacitynetwork.com</a>
      with the outlet or event name, the format, and the proposed date.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      For accuracy questions about anything published here, include the page URL and
      the source that contradicts it — see the
      <a href="/statistics">statistics page</a> for how claims are cited, and the
      <a href="/legal">corrections policy</a> for how fixes are handled.
    </p>
  </div>

  <EmailSignup compact />
</Base>
